      "message": "fix(ui,app): per-vise opening drafts; jaw body depth; review pins\n\nReview of PR #802:\n- Each built-in vise row keeps its own jaw-opening draft (a map by vise\n  name, State::vise_opening_draft). The single shared slot let two vise\n  rows reset each other every frame, so a value typed into the first was\n  lost and its Set sent the unchanged opening. The draft refreshes from\n  the live opening whenever that moves (Set, Open to stock, undo, redo)\n  and retires when the vise is deleted, renamed or no longer a vise.\n- A vise jaw is modelled as its whole body: a new jaw_body_depth (plate\n  included, at least the jaw thickness, default 2x it on every row)\n  extends each jaw's solid back along the screw up to jaw height, so\n  steel behind a plate below jaw height is struck. Editable in the\n  dialog, over MCP and in the file (absent reads as 2x the thickness).\n- Pins: two vise rows keep their own drafts; steel behind either plate\n  is struck on every size; undoing SetVise restores the old facets; a\n  nonsense vise key on load is dropped, logged and the steel kept.\n\nRefs #788\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
